cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "The Honest Backtest Census: How Often Famous Strategies Beat Buy & Hold"
abstract: >-
  An openly-licensed, aggregate snapshot of how 25 famous, named trading
  strategies performed against buy & hold across 36 liquid US stocks & ETFs over
  a fixed ~5-year window (frozen edition 2026-09-25). Of 839 strategy-asset
  backtests with enough trades to judge (of 900 combinations; 61 too thin and
  excluded), about 86% failed to beat buy & hold; ~14% beat. Net of trading
  costs and slippage, no look-ahead, against each asset's own buy & hold.
  Survivor-selected famous names; aggregate rates only (no per-trade records);
  one fixed window, no out-of-sample split; not significance-tested.
